/// An employé: somebody the school pays.
///
/// A staff row is *identity and employment*, and nothing else. What they are
/// paid, whether they turned up and what leave they took all belong to a period
/// — a contract, a month, a day — and therefore live on the four tables beside
/// this one. That is the same split as Student and Enrollment: a teacher who is
/// re-hired on a new contract has two contracts and one staff row, and last
/// year's payslips must keep resolving after this year's contract is signed.
///
/// ── Why this is not just a User ─────────────────────────────────────────────
/// A User is an *account*: somebody who signs in and holds permissions. Most of
/// the payroll never signs in — the driver, the concierge, the femme de ménage
/// — and some accounts are not employees at all. So `userId` is a nullable link
/// rather than the identity: the teacher who marks a register has both rows, the
/// gardien has only this one, and the caisse's audit trail keeps pointing at the
/// account that posted a movement rather than at an employment record.
///
/// Scoped to a school rather than the organisation, like Student and Vehicle: a
/// group's schools do their own hiring, run their own payroll and answer to
/// their own CNSS affiliation. Somebody genuinely shared between two schools is
/// two staff rows, which is also how the two payrolls stay separable.
model Staff {
  id       String @id @default(cuid())
  schoolId String
  school   School @relation(fields: [schoolId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  /// The account, when this person signs in. Nullable-unique: most employees
  /// have none, and no two may claim the same one.
  ///
  /// SetNull rather than Cascade — deleting an account must not delete an
  /// employment record with payslips hanging off it. The employment history is
  /// the school's; the login is only a convenience.
  userId String? @unique
  user   User?   @relation("StaffAccount", fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)

  /// Matricule interne, e.g. "P-2025-0007". Generated by the service layer when
  /// left blank, so every employee has a reference to write on a bulletin.
  code String

  firstName   String
  lastName    String
  /// Arabic given and family name. Contracts, attestations de travail and the
  /// CNSS declarations are issued in Arabic as well as French, and
  /// transliterating on the fly gets somebody's name wrong on a legal document.
  firstNameAr String?
  lastNameAr  String?

  /// "MALE" | "FEMALE" — see modules/students/enums.ts, which owns the list.
  /// Optional here, unlike a pupil's: nothing in payroll turns on it, and an
  /// employee file is often opened from a CV that does not say.
  gender String?

  birthDate  DateTime?
  birthPlace String?

  /// CIN — the number that appears on the contract and the CNSS declaration.
  nationalId String?

  /// Numéro d'immatriculation CNSS. Null until the affiliation comes back,
  /// which is weeks after somebody starts work.
  cnssNumber String?

  /// RIB, for salaries paid by virement. Stored as typed, not validated as a
  /// checksum: a bank detail that the bursar copied off a paper is worth
  /// keeping even when a digit is wrong, and refusing it just moves the number
  /// into a sticky note.
  bankRib String?

  phone   String?
  email   String?
  address String?

  /// "TEACHER" | "DIRECTOR" | ... — see modules/hr/enums.ts.
  ///
  /// One column rather than a role plus a department: the department is a
  /// consequence of the job (a driver is transport, a nurse is health) and
  /// storing both invites the two to disagree. `departmentOf` in enums.ts
  /// derives it.
  jobRole String @default("TEACHER")

  /// Free-text title as it appears on the contract — "Professeur de
  /// mathématiques", "Chauffeur de bus". `jobRole` is what the app groups and
  /// filters by; this is what the attestation prints.
  jobTitle String?

  /// Most minutes of class a week this employee may be given.
  ///
  /// A term of their employment, which is why it sits here and not in the
  /// school's settings: a full-timer, a part-timer and a vacataire are on
  /// different loads in the same school. Null falls back to the week's own
  /// ceiling — see `weekCapacityMinutes` in modules/timetable/service.ts — so
  /// a school that treats everyone the same never fills this in.
  ///
  /// Read by the timetable generator, which will not hand somebody a
  /// twenty-fifth hour. It does not stop a human doing so by hand: an
  /// exceptional week is the school's business, and a hard block would only be
  /// worked around by deleting the number.
  maxWeeklyMinutes Int?

  /// "ACTIVE" | "ON_LEAVE" | "SUSPENDED" | "TERMINATED" — see modules/hr/enums.ts.
  ///
  /// Typed in, unlike Student.status: leaving is a decision somebody makes and
  /// records, not something derivable from the contracts underneath. A contract
  /// that lapsed while a renewal is being signed must not quietly terminate an
  /// employee who is still coming to work.
  status String @default("ACTIVE")

  /// First day at this school, and the last. `hiredOn` is not derivable from
  /// the contracts: somebody promoted from a CDD to a CDI has a later contract
  /// start than their arrival, and seniority runs from the arrival.
  hiredOn DateTime?
  leftOn  DateTime?

  notes String?

  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

  contracts     EmploymentContract[]
  salaries      SalaryPayment[]
  /// Avances sur salaire — see prisma/schema/hr/salary-advance.prisma.
  advances      SalaryAdvance[]
  attendance    StaffAttendance[]
  leaveRequests LeaveRequest[]

  /// The buses this person drives. See the note on Vehicle.driverId.
  vehiclesDriven Vehicle[] @relation("VehicleDriver")

  /// The buses this person rides as accompagnateur. See Vehicle.attendantId.
  vehiclesAttended Vehicle[] @relation("VehicleAttendant")

  /// Fuel this person asked for. SetNull on the other side: a leaver must not
  /// take the fleet's spending history with them.
  fuelRequests FuelRequest[] @relation("FuelRequestedBy")

  /// Décaissements made out to this person — salaries, advances, reimbursed
  /// expenses. See the note on CashOperation.beneficiaryStaffId.
  paidOperations CashOperation[] @relation("OperationBeneficiaryStaff")

  @@unique([schoolId, code])
  @@index([schoolId])
  @@index([schoolId, lastName])
  @@index([schoolId, status])
  @@index([schoolId, jobRole])
  @@map("staff")
}
